{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_vrtx_011CfzuBQBwLiuR5M1ivw166", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I fixed the issue: Django's MySQL backend now passes mysqlclient the `database` and `password` keyword arguments instead of the deprecated `db` and `passwd`. The `dbshell` and `backends` test suites pass (278 tests, 90 skipped). They ran against SQLite, which isn't the MySQL connection path I changed, so the connection change hasn't been run against a real MySQL server.\n\n- **`django/db/backends/mysql/base.py`:** the connection settings now map `NAME` to `kwargs['database']` and `PASSWORD` to `kwargs['password']`.\n- **`django/db/backends/mysql/client.py`:** `dbshell` now reads `OPTIONS['database']` first, then falls back to `OPTIONS['db']`, then `NAME`. This matches how it already handled `password` before `passwd`, so existing settings keep working. I also renamed the local variable from `db` to `database`.\n\nThe docs (`docs/ref/databases.txt`, `docs/ref/settings.txt`) don't mention the old names, so they didn't need changes."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 196, "cache_read_input_tokens": 19768, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 196, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 360}, "input_transformations": [], "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a941d1f3-f6a1-411d-91dd-9922cb718742", "uuid": "2748935d-80fd-4142-b089-59b77ec198a7", "timestamp": "2026-10-13T20:53:37.073Z", "request_id": "req_vrtx_011CfzuBQ9DWUe8GMsrWed2D"}
